    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 45210,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45210.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "You know, I know there are times when there's a lot of talk about term limits, et cetera, but I would think somebody with some background and experience like yourself here in Congress, that would be a benefit to getting things done, would you think?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "There are times when people discuss term limits.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Some individuals have background and experience relevant to serving in Congress.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "A person with background and experience in Congress could help get things done.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The addressee has background and experience in Congress.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Experience in Congress is valuable for legislative effectiveness.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes the addressee is experienced in Congress.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Term limits discussions often overlook the value of institutional experience.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The addressee values being seen as effective in their role.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 45210,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45210.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Well, what's most important, I think, is the fact that elected representatives are not the sovereigns of our country. The sovereign of our country is the American people. Everybody that they elect is hired help, and it's their responsibility to watch that hired help very carefully between elections and then to weigh in during those elections is where they keep them or throw them out and hire some new help.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Elected representatives are not the sovereigns of our country.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The sovereign of our country is the American people.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Everyone that elected representatives elect are hired help.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "It is the responsibility of the American people to monitor elected officials between elections.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The American people have the power to decide whether to retain or replace elected officials during elections.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The legitimacy of political authority derives from popular sovereignty rather than institutional office.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Citizens possess sufficient agency and civic competence to effectively oversee government officials.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Regular democratic elections serve as meaningful mechanisms for accountability.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The metaphor of 'hired help' reflects a widely understood relationship between citizens and elected leaders.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Public oversight between elections is feasible and expected in a functioning democracy.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 45210,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45210.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "You're no stranger to the political world before coming to Washington. You spent 22 years in the California State Assembly having served both in the assembly and the Senate. You also ran for governor during the state's recall election in terms of goals and vision and personality. What's changed if anything with Tom McClintock since you first ran for office back in the early 80s?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
